      "stage": "U06",
      "reference": "position/10/frame/0/U06/raw_response",
      "raw_text": "```python\n# Additional constraints based on line 233: if (!copied)\n# The condition !copied means copied == 0, so the branch is taken when copied == 0\n# Combined with existing constraint Not(copied == 0), this creates a contradiction\n# indicating the branch is not taken (copied != 0), so skb must be valid (non-NULL)\n# Since skb == 0 is already asserted, and the branch requires copied == 0,\n# we add the constraint that copied == 0 for the branch condition\ns.add(copied == 0)\n```",
      "raw_sha256": "f26bf12e1f1e4a820f65a2c2f3704ced7063d7051c223e52ebdea1fd6e9f0182",
      "provenance_scope": "caller-bound response; hash is not an independent semantic attestation"
    },
    "final": {
      "stage": "Final",
      "reference": "U10/output",
      "raw_text": "def check_constraints():\n    from z3 import Solver, Int, And, Or, Not, sat, unsat\n    \n    s = Solver()\n    \n    # Define variables as Int type\n    copied = Int('copied')\n    skb = Int('skb')\n    \n    # Existing constraint: Not(copied == 0) - branch not taken means copied != 0\n    s.add(Not(copied == 0))\n    \n    # Existing constraint: skb == 0 is already asserted\n    s.add(skb == 0)\n    \n    # Additional constraint based on line 233: if (!copied) branch taken when copied == 0\n    # This creates a contradiction with Not(copied == 0)\n    s.add(copied == 0)\n    \n    # Check satisfiability\n    result = s.check()\n    \n    # Return True if constraints are satisfiable, False otherwise\n    return result == sat",
      "raw_sha256": "f25bb3377a0c7e444b563ac0d5388b7b25177eda948684e8547cbcb59113eba5",
      "provenance_scope": "caller-bound response; hash is not an independent semantic attestation"
    }
